    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Thundering Falls (which enters tapped) instead of casting Dragon's Rage Channeler or Monastery Swiftspear first is a sequencing error. With only 1 Mountain untapped and a hand full of cheap spells, playing a tapped land uses the entire turn doing nothing impactful. DRC would start surveiling to enable delirium and apply pressure, while Monastery Swiftspear would add another threat. The tapped land could be played on a later turn when the tempo cost is lower, or DRC could be cast first and then the tapped land played if no other one-mana play is available.",
