    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Gran-Gran (a creature) before playing a land drop is a sequencing error. The player has three fetchlands in hand (Polluted Delta, Scalding Tarn, Bloodstained Mire) and should play one first to ensure they don't miss their land drop this turn. Additionally, playing a fetchland first would enable Revolt for Fatal Push if needed later. More importantly, Psychic Frog is likely the stronger Turn 3 play here - it's a better threat that can grow, has evasion potential, and synergizes with the graveyard strategy alongside Emperor of Bones. Gran-Gran's card filtering is nice but its cost reduction ability requires three Lesson cards in graveyard which this deck likely won't achieve. Psychic Frog is the premier UB threat in Modern and should be prioritized.",
