    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The player is fetching a land (likely from Wooded Foothills, which searches for a Mountain or Forest). They already have a Mountain, Thundering Falls (Island Mountain), and Steam Vents (Island Mountain) on the battlefield. Fetching a basic Mountain would be better here - it comes into play untapped for free (no life payment), whereas Steam Vents requires paying 2 life to enter untapped. With the opponent at 16 life and the player at 18 life holding aggressive creatures and Lightning Bolt, every point of life matters but so does mana efficiency. However, the player already has red sources covered by Mountain and could benefit from having additional blue mana for future Spell Pierces or other blue spells. That said, fetching basic Mountain preserves 2 life (or avoids entering tapped) and the player already has blue from Thundering Falls and Steam Vents. The basic Mountain is almost certainly correct here since they have plenty of blue sources already and don't need to pay 2 life for another dual land.",
