    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Thoughtseize before playing a land and before combat is a sequencing consideration. The opponent has only Monastery Swiftspear on board with one untapped land (Mountain is tapped), while MiniMx Gramps has Emperor of Bones and Psychic Frog. More importantly, Thoughtseize costs 2 life (going from 16 to 14), and the opponent has an aggressive deck. Playing a fetch land first (Polluted Delta, Scalding Tarn, or Bloodstained Mire) would enable revolt for Fatal Push, which could kill creatures with mana value 4 or less. Additionally, if the opponent's hand is mostly lands or low-impact cards, the Thoughtseize may not be worth the life loss at this stage. However, getting information and stripping a key card before combat and before the opponent untaps fully is reasonable. The main concern is sequencing - playing a fetch land first before Thoughtseize would be better since it doesn't cost anything and keeps revolt available for Fatal Push if needed during combat or in response to something.",
