    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Cori-Steel Cutter (a non-creature spell) before combat is suboptimal when Monastery Swiftspear is on the battlefield. Swiftspear has prowess, so casting noncreature spells before combat would pump it +1/+1 for the attack. However, the bigger issue is sequencing: casting the equipment before combat telegraphs the plan and gives the opponent information. More importantly, if the player plans to cast a second spell this turn to trigger Cori-Steel Cutter's flurry ability (creating a 1/1 Monk token that can be equipped), they should consider whether Lightning Bolt targeting the opponent or a blocker before combat might be more impactful. The Cori-Steel Cutter does trigger prowess on Swiftspear, which is good before combat, but casting Dragon's Rage Channeler first (a creature, no prowess trigger) and then the equipment as the second spell would trigger flurry and create a token. The sequencing of casting a noncreature spell before combat is actually correct for prowess on Swiftspear, but the player should consider whether Lightning Bolt (which also triggers prowess AND deals 3 damage or removes a blocker) would be better as the pre-combat spell, saving the equipment for post-combat or as the second spell for flurry.",
